##gtf-version 2.2
##description THE METHOD-DEVELOPMENT TEST TRANSCRIPTOME — hand-edited, one structure at a time.
##
## ⭐⭐⭐ THIS FILE IS THE BENCHMARK (owner, 2026-08-19): the test chromosome, this GTF and
## `test_abundances.tsv` comprise the method-development benchmark. The FASTA and everything
## downstream are DERIVED — `build_test_reference.py`, then `docs/TESTING.md` §0a.
##
## ── THE ANCHORED TWIN BLOCK (owner design, 2026-08-28) ─────────────────────────────────
## ONE shape everywhere: exon 1 kb · intron 7 kb · exon 1 kb · intron 7 kb · exon 1 kb
## (span 17,000 bp), 20 kb intergenic between genes, all + strand. FIVE gene types varying
## exactly one bit each, repeated in FIVE abundance blocks (B1..B5) = 25 transcripts:
##
##   clean    unprobed, no nascent — intron + flanks exactly pure gDNA; one certified SJ/intron
##   nasc     unprobed, nascent ON — the contaminated message source (intron is not pure gDNA)
##   cap      probed,   no nascent — the enrichment cliff between source and destination
##   capnasc  probed,   nascent ON — both at once
##   silent   probed,   mrna = 0  — every object pure gDNA; any claimed RNA is a false positive
##
## Abundances live in `test_abundances.tsv` (⛔ that file takes no comments — both its readers
## key on the first line — so its design is recorded here). Molar ladders, half-decade steps,
## mature UP the blocks and nascent DOWN — independent levels, as the big ladder draws them:
##
##   block:            B1    B2    B3    B4    B5
##   mrna_abundance:   10    30   100   300  1000    (clean/nasc/cap/capnasc; silent = 0)
##   nrna_abundance:  100    30    10     3     1    (nasc/capnasc only; all others = 0)
##
## In FRAGMENT terms the nascent entity spans 17 kb against 3 kb spliced, so the per-gene
## nascent:mature fragment ratio is ≈ 5.67·nrna/mrna = 57 / 5.7 / 0.57 / 0.057 / 0.0057 across
## B1..B5 — far-above, above, near, below, far-below mature. Library-wide nascent is ~22 % of
## RNA fragments off capture, matching the big ladder's stress burden (`DESIGN.md` §0b: a
## STRESS level, not real data; realistic is ~4 %).
##
## Probes live in `test_probes.bed` and tile PER EXON, abutting both exon ends (a probe
## spanning an sj would suppress exactly the boundary-crossing gDNA — `docs/TESTING.md` §0b).
##
## The question this substrate answers: on unstranded rows, is the information a blind exon
## needs actually present in its neighbours — split by source quality (clean vs nasc) and by
## frame (uncaptured vs the capture cliff) — and on stranded rows, does a policy leave the
## sighted solve alone?  (`ISSUES: message-value-for-blind-slots`.)
##
## FORMAT: one `exon` line per exon, GTF 1-based inclusive coordinates.
##   test_chr  rigel_test  exon  START  END  .  STRAND  .  gene_id "gX"; transcript_id "TX";
